  "title": "Qt: Lower FilterEdit debounce timer",
  "description": "The generally accepted principle for UI response time is 100 ms for\nsomething to feel instantaneous.[1, 2] Lower the debounce timer from\n150 ms to 75 ms so that the background update does not appear to lag\nbehind the input.\n\nFix #21314.\n\n[1] - Robert B. Miller. 1968. Response time in man-computer\nconversational transactions. In Proceedings of the December 9-11, 1968,\nfall joint computer conference, part I (AFIPS '68), San Francisco, California.\nACM Inc., New York, NY, 267-277. https://doi.org/10.1145/1476589.1476628\n[2] - Stuart K. Card, George G. Robertson, Jock D. Mackinlay. 1981.\nThe information visualizer, an information workspace. In Proceedings of\nthe SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems (CHI '91),\nNew Orleans, Louisiana. ACM Inc., New York, NY, 181-186.\nhttps://doi.org/10.1145/108844.108874\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
